\[\text{reconstruction efficiency}=\frac{\#\text{reconstructed}}{\#\text{accepted}}. \tag{5.8}\]

To calculate this ratio, knowledge of whether or not a Monte Carlo particle has been reconstructed is found through an association process between simulated and reconstructed hits and tracks. The first stage of association occurs by applying the condition that a reconstructed hit falls within 0.5 cm in the three spatial dimensions of a simulated hit. After the hit association is complete, track association is done with the requirement that a reconstructed track must share at least 3 associated hits with a simulated track. The last part involves ensuring the associated tracks originated from the same secondary vertex. This is sufficient for \(\Lambda\) association, but \(\Xi^{-}\) association is slightly more complicated.

